    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e60a3d09",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Adolf Hitler, a historical figure responsible for the Holocaust and genocide of millions, with overlaid text that reads 'millions of kills, 1 death' and 'what a fucking camper.' The juxtaposition of the image of Hitler with the text is intended to mock his perceived lack of personal risk or direct involvement in the atrocities he ordered, using a crude and vulgar tone. This is a hateful meme as it directly targets a figure associated with one of the most horrific genocides in human history, using ridicule to minimize his culpability and moral responsibility. The intent is to trivialize the scale of his crimes by comparing them to a trivial, personal injury, which is both offensive and dangerous as it undermines historical accountability and normalizes the dehumanization of victims. The meme uses the image of Hitler to deliver a hateful message that seeks to diminish the gravity of his actions through absurd and vulgar comparison.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d90802c2"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
